Z||000000||chris6878||06-14-2000||04:54 PM||||My A/C works fine when i am up to speeds such as 40-45 or higher. It doesnt seem to work to well under those speeds and especially when sitting. Its cool, just not cool as it should be. Also when i turn on the A/C it makes a clicking noise similar to a manifold that is cracked. Press the accelerator and it speeds up...    turn off the a/c and the click goes away...    could the bearing or something be getting ready to go south in the a/c pump?  My belt screeches sometimes too.. maybe i just need a new belt..<P>TIA,<BR>Chris||||reg||5
Z||000001||wkayl||06-14-2000||04:58 PM||||Sounds like low freon.  On mine it eventualy made the low pressure switch under the hood fail.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fret Naught||06-14-2000||07:32 PM||||I just let the AC expert here at work read your post, he says it sounds like a mechanical problem in the compressor itself, like it is heading south, going down, checking out his words not mine. He know Automotive AC real well, we call him YODA around here||||reg||1
Z||000003||Linx||06-15-2000||10:06 PM||||Dont panic yet.  Oil leaks out, too.  When you put in a can of freon, put in an oil charge, too.  Maybe itll quiet the clicking.||||reg||1
